## Verdict: **APPROVED**

### Executive Summary

Commit `0726414` remediates all 8 round-1 findings faithfully. `releaseClaim` restores the per-source coverage row verbatim (watermark, indexed_at, error, history_truncated, prior status) on both release paths — the exact defect that wiped state now preserves it, including the `!exists` honest-empty-row case. Tokenview's `headStalled` boundary eliminates the unearned join: `fin` requires a *proven* `st.head >= ToBlock`, stalled scans emit nothing, carry no continuation, and don't re-burn at the same/larger window. The three regression tests are honest — real DB rows, real wire shapes, defect-condition assertions — and all pass. The only new finding is a narrow pre-existing TOCTOU: `releaseClaim` can stale-restore over a concurrent terminal write (understate-only, fail-safe direction).

### Round-1 finding verification

