### New findings

**[Minor] `releaseClaim` stale-restore can regress a concurrent terminal write (advisory-claim TOCTOU)** — `MarkWalletIndexing` is an unconditional upsert (`ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE SET status='indexing'`), not a claim-CAS. A second process that read state before a concurrent claim proceeds to `attemptFetch`; its `releaseClaim` then writes its stale pre-claim `st.row` over the first process's terminal write (e.g., watermark 900→400). Window: loadState→release (~1 head call). Direction is strictly *understate* — coverage regresses, never over-claims — so it self-heals on next refresh. Intra-process is closed by `singleflight`; exposure needs multi-replica deployment + head-lag. The same TOCTOU class exists at every write site and predates this remediation (the old code NULL-wiped in the same race — strictly worse). If multi-replica operation is planned, a conditional release (`UPDATE ... WHERE status='indexing'`) would close it. Not a blocker.

**[Nit]** Moralis strict `atoi` has no dedicated regression test (minor fix; "12x"/""/negative rows).

**[Nit]** `headBlocked` calls still consume 1 prepaid budget unit for 0 upstream calls — conservative over-charge, bounded.

**[Nit]** `case srcID == 0: continue` (service.go:256) is now unreachable (srcID==0 only when `adapter==nil`, caught by the earlier gate) — harmless defensive residue.

**[Nit]** Remediation report n1 claims tatum/chainbase "partition on Kinds" — they don't read `opts.Kinds` (consumers are alchemy/nodereal/chainscan). The code fix is correct; the justification names wrong adapters.

**[Nit]** Bitquery test fixture marks native rows `Fungible: !native` = false — real BNB rows are fungible. Inert: the filter only gates the token stream.

